@annevk, @domenic, this isn't quite ready to land yet as there are still a few open questions to sort out (at least https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/1087 and https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/1093), plus missing implementor positions. But I don't expect most of the mechanics in this PR to change, so I think it would be great to get feedback on whether the approach we've used here is agreeable.

See also https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1353

Thanks!

@annevk , @keithamus, @smaug----, this is ready for another round of review. I'd like to see if Chromium can ship this soon, so I want to make sure any remaining concerns are captured first. Thanks!

Note that I've incorporated the event propagation change discussed in https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/1098 into this PR.

cc @alice

> The [composed flag](https://github.com/dandclark/html/blob/229c48dd6d9801457f674165bd62a6c8725a6f9d/source#L65267) is now set unconditionally on submit, toggle, and beforetoggle (six more sites follow the same pattern). When there is no source or submitter, relatedTarget is null, so these events now escape shadow trees. This affects showPopover(), hidePopover(), light dismiss, showModal(), and requestSubmit() without a submitter. Chromium only sets composed when there is an invoker, source, or submitter. The earlier AI feedback that called a conditional composed flag a blocker was wrong: with the relatedTarget model, an event whose source is in the same tree still stops at the shadow boundary. Consider a helper that sets relatedTarget and composed only for a non-null source, plus WPTs for the sourceless cases.

IIUC, a testcase for the unconditioned composed flag would be like this:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<div id="host">
  <template shadowrootmode="open">
    <form>
      <input type="text" value="press enter">
    </form>
  </template>
</div>
<script>
const shadowRoot = document.querySelector('#host').shadowRoot;
const form = shadowRoot.querySelector('form');

form.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
  event.preventDefault();
  console.log(event.composed);
  console.log(event.submitter);
  console.log(event.composedPath());
});
host.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
  alert("Event escaped shadow root!");
});
</script>
```
